<ArticleLayout slug="stock-photos-vs-ai-images" ctaLabel="Create your account" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">For product content, the choice isn't really stock or AI. It's whether the picture has to show your product. A stock photo can't, and neither can an image generated from a sentence. An AI edit of your own product photo can.</p>

  <h2>Stock photos vs AI images: which should you use for product content?</h2>

  <p>Use licensed stock for real places, real events and documentary scenes. Use text-to-image for props, moods and backgrounds that hold no product. When the product itself must appear, edit your own product photo into the new scene, in an app like hubStudio or any editor that takes a source picture. Stock licenses cap use. Generated work carries thinner copyright.</p>

